# printer-quirks.ti59 Program that demonstrates interrupting the printer while printing a row.
# From Magatzine "PPX Exchange", March/April 1982, page 5.
#
# These are the original notes in the article:
#  The following program (reprinted with permission) by Dave Leising produces a print-code table with the characters
#  printed as they appear normally and as they appear after an immediate interrupt. Note: all printers may not print the
#  same portion of the characters. On our printers, they appear as shown.
#
#  Initialize the pseudo-code by pressing the sequence: [9] [2nd] [OP] [1] [7] [2nd] [Pgm] [1] [2] [SBR] [4] [4] [4]
#  [R/S] [2nd] [P/R] [LRN] [2nd] [Ins] [LRN] [CLR] [RST].
#  The display will begin flashing when [SBR] [4] [4] [4] is pressed. Press [A] and the print code table with full and inter-
#  rupted characters will be printed.

MODEL: TI-59
SOLID-STATE-MODULE: ML
PRINTER: on


# For compactness, the program is only here as key codes. If you need the listing, load the program and LIST it on the printer.
PROGRAM:
92 00 00 76 11 00 69 05 23 53  00 00 00 00 00 00 00 69 17 58   # 000-019
09 25 69 00 06 06 07 06 07 06  07 01 00 69 02 11 02 07 00 00   # 020-039
00 00 00 00 02 05 69 02 11 11  01 00 00 69 03 11 00 69 03 11   # 040-059
02 05 00 00 02 07 69 03 11 00  69 03 11 06 06 00 00 69 03 11   # 060-079
00 69 03 11 02 07 58 08 69 02  11 07 00 69 03 11 05 06 58 06   # 080-099
69 03 11 05 01 58 08 69 04 58  04 07 05 01 69 03 11 06 07 04   # 100-119
07 69 04 58 09 07 04 07 04 07  04 06 07 69 03 11 04 07 58 04   # 120-139
69 04 58 02 07 04 07 04 07 04  69 03 11 11 05 07 04 06 07 07   # 140-159
04 69 03 11 07 02 04 00 00 00  07 69 03 11 07 04 05 06 00 00   # 160-179
02 04 07 04 69 03 32 58 04 02  07 00 00 04 07 69 04 02 07 00   # 180-199
00 00 00 05 05 07 04 69 02 75  11 05 00 00 00 95 69 02 32 85   # 200-219
05 00 00 00 95 69 03 11 32 85  06 00 00 00 05 69 02 75 11 03   # 220-239
05 00 00 95 69 02 85 07 04 02  07 00 00 07 04 07 04 69 03 11   # 240-259
05 01 04 00 00 95 69 02 06 02  69 04 11 07 04 00 00 05 03 07   # 260-279
04 07 04 69 03 02 05 69 04 58  09 07 04 07 04 69 02 07 06 07   # 280-299
06 07 06 07 06 07 69 01 11 00  69 04 04 07 58 08 69 01 07 04   # 300-319
00 00 02 05 07 04 07 04 69 03  75 11 05 03 69 01 02 07 58 02   # 320-339
69 04 11 07 04 07 04 95 58 04  69 03 85 00 69 02 05 06 58 06   # 340-359
69 01 11 05 06 00 00 95 69 03  04 07 69 03 11 05 03 69 01 07   # 360-379
00 00 00 05 02 07 58 02 69 03  11 02 00 00 06 05 02 07 69 03   # 380-399
05 06 58 04 69 01 11 04 07 69  01 05 06 00 00 06 05 69 03 75   # 400-419
04 01 03 95 69 03 05 03 69 01  58 09 69 02 11 00 69 01 02 05   # 420-439
69 02 02 07 00 00 07 04 00 00  00 00 69 03 11 05 69 02 11 69   # 440-459
04 05 06 00 00 69 01 06 05 69  02 07 04 07 04 07 04 58 04 69   # 460-479
03 95 58 02 04 07 69 01 58 04  05 05 69 04 11 58 02 02 05 69   # 480-499
01 05 03 06 07 07 01 00 00 06  05 69 02 58 06 05 03 69 04 11   # 500-519
07 04 07 04 07 04 07 04 69 03  75 04 07 69 04 58 04 00 69 01   # 520-539
06 05 69 02 11 02 07 69 01 07  00 00 00 00 02 07 06 05 69 02   # 540-559
05 03 02 07 58 06 69 04 11 07  02 95 69 03 05 58 02 05 06 69   # 560-579
01 02 07 00 00 00 00 02 07 02  05 69 02 04 07 58 08 69 04 11   # 580-599
02 07 69 04 58 07 05 03 69 01  58 02 05 06 69 02 05 04 95 69   # 600-619
03 11 69 00 04 07 69 02 07 04  07 04 07 04 02 07 05 03 69 03   # 620-639
44 06 00 07 04 07 04 00 00 00  07 69 03 11 06 02 69 02 05 03   # 640-659
07 04 07 07 00 00 02 07 69 03  11 05 03 69 02 69 03 11 04 07   # 660-679
58 03 11 69 02 11 58 09 69 00  05 08 69 02 58 02 01 00 00 69   # 680-699
03 04 07 69 02 11 05 03 58 02  11 69 02 58 02 05 06 58 03 01   # 700-719
05 06 00 00 00 00 04 07 69 03  11 05 03 00 01 07 00 04 07 69   # 720-739
03 95 91 05 00 00 07 02 07 03  11 05 03 00 00 05 03 69 03 95   # 740-759
06 07 06 07 69 03 11 58 09 98  98 98 92 61 00 07 17 00 00 00   # 760-779

# To simplify things, the keystrokes outlined in the article are automated. When the Preset finished loading, the invalid
# key code will be in memory.
# KEYSTROKES:
# 61  GTO
# 92  0
# 92  0
# 63  8
# 64  9
# 21  2nd
# 64  OP
# 82  1
# 62  7
# 21  2nd
# 31  Pgm
# 82  1
# 83  2
# 71  SBR
# 72  4
# 72  4
# 72  4
# Wait: 1s
# 91  R/S
# WaitFullSpeed: 1s
# 21  2nd
# 32  P/R
# 31  LRN
# 21  2nd
# 41  Ins
# 31  LRN
# 25  CLR
# 81  RST
